###
---
name: my-kobo-skill
description: 'Check to see if a directory has kobo files in it'
---

The following is a full listing of the cabapilities of 
this skill.  It uses kobo to enable its functionality

## Options
this skill can do a few things.  All things are done by telling the agent what to do.  It
will determine the appropriate command line to pass into this program based on that.  
The script is located in scripts/12.simplekoboskill.kobo.  When the right command is determined
it triggers the following script to be called
kobo run -source scripts/scripts/12.simplekoboskill.kobo -- (put the command you dermine should be invoked here)




###
#:script

if(args.Length > 0)
{
    var command = args[0]
    Print("we have arguments: ${command}")

    switch (command)
    {
        case "hello":
            Print("say hello")
            break;
        case "work":
            Print("do the work of the skill")
            break;
    }

}else
{
    Print("cant do anything")
}

###
# IGNORED BY AGENT 
This section is not read by the agent.  
To publish this skill: 

1. Create a new folder named **my-kobo-skill** inside of your agentic platform's ```skills``` folder
2. Create a new folder named **scripts** inside of your ```skills``` folder
3. run ```kobo generate --source 12.simplekoboskill.kobo --markdown SKILLS.md```
4. Copy the SKILLS.md file produced as an output to **my-kobo-skill**
5. Copy the kobo file to **my-kobo-skill/scripts**
6. In your agent prompt window type ```/my-kobo-skill send me a greeting``` or some other prompt that will
make the agent resolve the request to the hello prompt

> NOTE:  This is just a simple example.  A more appropriate mechanism might be to have the agent pass a json inot
the skill, then the skill could parse the request and respond accordingly
